{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":125222}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/mubashirulhassan00/predicting-stellar-class-s6e6-catboost-auc-96?scriptVersionId=325261852\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<style>\n@keyframes glow {\n  0%, 100% { text-shadow: 0 0 10px #7B68EE, 0 0 20px #7B68EE, 0 0 40px #7B68EE; }\n  50% { text-shadow: 0 0 20px #9B88FF, 0 0 40px #9B88FF, 0 0 80px #9B88FF; }\n}\n@keyframes slideUp {\n  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); }\n  to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n}\n@keyframes shimmer {\n  0% { background-position: -200% center; }\n  100% { background-position: 200% center; }\n}\n@keyframes twinkle {\n  0%, 100% { opacity: 0.3; }\n  50% { opacity: 1; }\n}\n@keyframes pulse {\n  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); }\n  50% { transform: scale(1.05); }\n}\n</style>\n\n<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a0a2e 0%, #1a1a4e 50%, #2d1b69 100%); padding: 40px; border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid #7B68EE; margin-bottom: 20px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\">\n\n<div style=\"position: absolute; top: 15px; left: 25px; animation: twinkle 2s ease-in-out infinite;\">✦</div>\n<div style=\"position: absolute; top: 40px; right: 60px; animation: twinkle 3s ease-in-out infinite 0.5s; color: #FFE66D; font-size: 0.6em;\">✦</div>\n<div style=\"position: absolute; bottom: 30px; left: 80px; animation: twinkle 2.5s ease-in-out infinite 1s; color: #4ECDC4; font-size: 0.5em;\">✦</div>\n<div style=\"position: absolute; top: 60px; left: 50%; animation: twinkle 4s ease-in-out infinite 1.5s; color: #FF6B6B; font-size: 0.4em;\">✦</div>\n<div style=\"position: absolute; bottom: 20px; right: 120px; animation: twinkle 3.5s ease-in-out infinite 0.8s; color: #7B68EE; font-size: 0.7em;\">✦</div>\n\n<h1 style=\"color: #e0e0ff; text-align: center; font-size: 2.5em; margin-bottom: 5px; animation: glow 3s ease-in-out infinite, slideUp 1s ease-out;\">🌌 Predicting Stellar Class</h1>\n\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; font-size: 1.2em; margin-top: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #7B68EE, #FF6B6B, #FFE66D, #4ECDC4, #7B68EE); background-size: 200% auto; -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; background-clip: text; animation: shimmer 4s linear infinite, slideUp 1.2s ease-out;\">Playground Series — Season 6, Episode 6</h3>\n\n<p style=\"color: #b0b0d0; text-align: center; font-size: 1em; animation: slideUp 1.4s ease-out;\">A comprehensive EDA, feature engineering & CatBoost modeling notebook</p>\n\n<hr style=\"border: 1px solid #7B68EE; margin: 20px 50px;\">\n\n<p style=\"color: #9090c0; text-align: center; font-size: 0.9em; animation: slideUp 1.6s ease-out;\">\n🎯 <b>Objective:</b> Multi-class classification of celestial objects (GALAXY, STAR, QSO)<br>\n📏 <b>Metric:</b> Balanced Accuracy &nbsp;|&nbsp; 📊 <b>Data:</b> Synthetic (based on SDSS17)<br>\n🧠 <b>Model:</b> CatBoost with Optuna HPO &nbsp;|&nbsp; 🚀 <b>GPU:</b> T4 Accelerated\n</p>\n\n</div>\n","metadata":{"_uuid":"efa172b8-9cc7-4751-af72-3ddae39b978e","_cell_guid":"14b8aa42-1aad-4bcf-8abb-6522e6b62f3f","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 📑 Table of Contents\n\n| # | Section | Description |\n|---|---------|-------------|\n| 1 | [🔧 Setup & Configuration](#setup) | Imports, seeds, global settings |\n| 2 | [📥 Data Loading & First Look](#data-loading) | Load files, shape, dtypes, missing values |\n| 3 | [🎯 Target Analysis](#target-analysis) | Class distribution & imbalance check |\n| 4 | [📊 Univariate EDA](#univariate-eda) | Feature distributions by class |\n| 5 | [🔗 Bivariate & Multivariate EDA](#bivariate-eda) | Correlations, scatter plots, pairplots |\n| 6 | [🔬 Advanced Visualizations](#advanced-viz) | t-SNE embedding, parallel coordinates |\n| 7 | [🛠️ Feature Engineering](#feature-engineering) | Color indices, magnitude stats, interactions |\n| 8 | [🏗️ Preprocessing](#preprocessing) | Label encoding, feature selection, CV setup |\n| 9 | [🤖 Model Training & Tuning](#model-training) | Optuna HPO for LGB, XGB, CatBoost |\n| 10 | [📈 Model Diagnostics](#diagnostics) | SHAP, confusion matrix, learning curves |\n| 11 | [📤 Submission](#submission) | Ensemble predictions & submission file |","metadata":{"_uuid":"d50ccc02-1e7e-4ec3-8f05-9b8e759d1a8b","_cell_guid":"55132530-53fb-4e69-a04f-954c3a13337b","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 🌠 Astrophysics Primer\n\nThis competition asks us to classify **celestial objects** observed by the [Sloan Digital Sky Survey (SDSS)](https://www.sdss.org/) into three categories:\n\n| Class | What is it? | Key Characteristics |\n|-------|------------|---------------------|\n| **GALAXY** 🌀 | A gravitationally bound system of stars, gas, dust, and dark matter | Moderate redshift, broad spectral features |\n| **STAR** ⭐ | A luminous sphere of plasma held together by gravity | Very low/zero redshift, sharp spectral lines |\n| **QSO** 💫 | Quasi-Stellar Object (Quasar) — an extremely luminous active galactic nucleus | High redshift, point-like appearance |\n\n### Key Features from SDSS Photometry\n- **Photometric bands (u, g, r, i, z):** Magnitudes measured through 5 optical filters spanning ultraviolet to infrared\n- **Redshift:** Measures how much the light wavelength has been stretched — directly relates to distance and velocity\n- **Right Ascension (alpha) & Declination (delta):** Celestial coordinates (like longitude & latitude on the sky)\n- **Color indices (u-g, g-r, r-i, i-z):** Differences between adjacent band magnitudes — crucial for classification\n\n> 💡 **Redshift is typically the single most discriminative feature** — Stars have ~0 redshift, Galaxies have moderate redshift, and Quasars have high redshift.","metadata":{"_uuid":"b3a14cdf-23b7-45fa-94b8-e1793d7153e6","_cell_guid":"098cf24c-ac61-408e-9844-5bb2b19968dd","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<a id=\"setup\"></a>\n## 1. 🔧 Setup & Configuration","metadata":{"_uuid":"0029cf66-edb6-42f0-8caa-b7b75c0a8033","_cell_guid":"b36f721e-38b0-41ab-a75f-fa939327104b","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec\nimport seaborn as sns\nfrom matplotlib.colors import LinearSegmentedColormap\nimport plotly.express as px\nimport plotly.graph_objects as go\nfrom plotly.subplots import make_subplots\nimport plotly.io as pio\n\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (\n    balanced_accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix,\n    roc_auc_score, roc_curve, auc, precision_recall_curve,\n    average_precision_score\n)\nfrom sklearn.manifold import TSNE\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import learning_curve\n\nimport lightgbm as lgb\nimport xgboost as xgb\nfrom catboost import CatBoostClassifier, Pool\n\nimport optuna\nfrom optuna.samplers import TPESampler\noptuna.logging.set_verbosity(optuna.logging.WARNING)\n\nimport shap\nimport warnings\nimport os\nimport gc\nimport time\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\nprint(\"✅ All libraries imported successfully!\")","metadata":{"_uuid":"5486b1a3-a712-42a7-952e-0feb49f8937d","_cell_guid":"e2d05da6-50b1-4b55-a33b-9a99e1b5f344","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-07T20:19:18.004813Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-07T20:19:18.005336Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.647742Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-07T20:19:18.005303Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.647032Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"✅ All libraries imported successfully!\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# CONFIGURATION\n# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nclass CFG:\n    \"\"\"Central configuration — adjust these knobs as needed.\"\"\"\n    SEED = 42\n    N_FOLDS = 5                   # Stratified K-Fold splits\n    OPTUNA_TRIALS = 30            # Trials per model (increase for better tuning)\n    OPTUNA_CV_FOLDS = 3           # Folds used during Optuna search (faster)\n    EARLY_STOPPING = 100          # Early stopping patience\n    USE_ORIGINAL_DATA = False     # Set True & add SDSS17 dataset to Kaggle inputs\n    USE_GPU = True                # Set True if running with GPU accelerator\n    TSNE_SAMPLE = 8000            # Subsample size for t-SNE (speed)\n    SHAP_SAMPLE = 1500            # Subsample size for SHAP (speed)\n\nnp.random.seed(CFG.SEED)\n\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# VISUALIZATION THEME — dark space aesthetic\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nplt.style.use('dark_background')\nplt.rcParams.update({\n    'figure.figsize': (14, 6),\n    'figure.dpi': 100,\n    'axes.facecolor': '#0d1117',\n    'figure.facecolor': '#0d1117',\n    'axes.edgecolor': '#30363d',\n    'axes.labelcolor': '#c9d1d9',\n    'xtick.color': '#8b949e',\n    'ytick.color': '#8b949e',\n    'text.color': '#c9d1d9',\n    'axes.grid': True,\n    'grid.color': '#21262d',\n    'grid.alpha': 0.6,\n    'font.family': 'sans-serif',\n    'font.size': 11,\n})\n\n# Class color palette — consistent throughout the notebook\nCLASS_COLORS = {'GALAXY': '#FF6B6B', 'STAR': '#4ECDC4', 'QSO': '#FFE66D'}\nCLASS_PALETTE = list(CLASS_COLORS.values())\nACCENT = '#7B68EE'\n\n# Custom colormap for heatmaps\nspace_cmap = LinearSegmentedColormap.from_list(\n    'space', ['#0d1117', '#1a1a4e', '#7B68EE', '#FF6B6B', '#FFE66D']\n)\n\nprint(f\"🔧 Configuration loaded | Seed={CFG.SEED} | Folds={CFG.N_FOLDS} | Optuna trials={CFG.OPTUNA_TRIALS}\")","metadata":{"_uuid":"77c59821-39fa-402e-8f32-ee5b0956d999","_cell_guid":"ad71450b-a190-44d7-8c96-7c0c281871a8","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.649077Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.649668Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.659881Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.649645Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.658696Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"🔧 Configuration loaded | Seed=42 | Folds=5 | Optuna trials=30\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<a id=\"data-loading\"></a>\n## 2. 📥 Data Loading & First Look","metadata":{"_uuid":"ec170b0a-5602-4ef9-b48d-01bca2528cab","_cell_guid":"cb312bd6-f34f-46f2-bdb5-370a92de07b1","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# LOAD DATA\n# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nINPUT_DIR = '/kaggle/input/competitions/playground-series-s6e6'\n\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f'{INPUT_DIR}/train.csv')\ntest = pd.read_csv(f'{INPUT_DIR}/test.csv')\nsample_sub = pd.read_csv(f'{INPUT_DIR}/sample_submission.csv')\n\nprint(f\"📦 Train shape : {train.shape}\")\nprint(f\"📦 Test shape  : {test.shape}\")\nprint(f\"📦 Submission  : {sample_sub.shape}\")\nprint(f\"\\n📋 Train columns ({len(train.columns)}):\\n{list(train.columns)}\")","metadata":{"_uuid":"0cb4c98d-bdc5-4fe7-a3ca-a5932d32e5f9","_cell_guid":"4e89dbd7-ff6b-43df-ab4a-b409f3dba40c","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.660903Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.661678Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-07T20:19:35.94927Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-07T20:19:33.661654Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-07T20:19:35.948373Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"📦 Train shape : (577347, 12)\n📦 Test shape  : (247435, 11)\n📦 Submission  : (247435, 2)\n\n📋 Train columns (12):\n['id', 'alpha', 'delta', 'u', 'g', 'r', 'i', 'z', 'redshift', 'spectral_type', 'galaxy_population', 'class']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DATA TYPES & INFO\n# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nprint(\"═\" * 70)\nprint(\"DATA TYPES SUMMARY\")\nprint(\"═\" * 70)\n\ndtype_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    'Column': train.columns,\n    'Type': train.dtypes.values,\n    'Non-Null': train.notnull().sum().values,\n    'Null': train.isnull().sum().values,\n    'Null %': (train.isnull().sum().values / len(train) * 100).round(2),\n    'Unique': train.nunique().values,\n    'Sample': [train[c].iloc[0] for c in train.columns]\n})\nprint(dtype_df.to_string(index=False))","metadata":{"_uuid":"928cfa2d-6319-4e48-9565-e2d5dff74b2c","_cell_guid":"768e3cad-27aa-4e38-b666-64b6166976eb","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-07T20:19:35.950765Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-07T20:19:35.950981Z","iopub.status.idle":"